# A stale tab that's held a page open across a deploy will still ask for an old build's hashed
# asset filename (e.g. /assets/index-OLDHASH.js), which no longer exists once a newer deploy
# replaces it. Without this line, the catch-all below used to swallow that into index.html -
# served with status 200 and a text/html MIME type - which the browser's module-script loader
# correctly refuses to execute as JS ("Expected a JavaScript-or-Wasm module script but the server
# responded with a MIME type of text/html"), leaving a blank page with no visible error for
# anything client-side to recover from. This makes a missing asset a real 404 instead, which
# index.html's own inline bootstrap script (see index.html) catches and recovers from with one
# reload.
/assets/* /assets/:splat 404

/* /index.html 200
